# fuzz-lab local state. Nothing here is source.

# Run artefacts. `out/last-run.json` is a report of one run on one machine: its timings
# and counts are regenerated by the loop and are not properties of the tree.
out/

#
# A crashing input is a reproducer, not an artifact: it is the one file in this lab
# that must never be committed. Two reasons, and both are real.
#
#   1. The root .gitignore already excludes *.pcap, *.pf and friends, so a reproducer
#      for the pcap or prefetch target would be silently untracked -- and a crash you
#      cannot name is a crash nobody fixes.
#   2. A reproducer is hostile input. Committing hostile input into a repository that
#      ships parsers for it is how a "harmless test corpus" becomes the thing that
#      breaks the next person who runs the parsers over the tree.
#
# What IS committed is the recipe: `crashes/index.json` records the sha256, the byte
# length, the seed it came from, the mutation strategy chain, and the exact command to
# re-derive it. `tools/replay.mjs <sha256-prefix>` rebuilds the file from the recipe and
# confirms the hash matches, so the reproducer is reconstructible without being stored.
crashes/
